AArch64 arm64-userword-lostpublish-fixed
(* Same protocol and same condition as arm64-userword-lostpublish-main, with the
   fix's handover.

   The release store on localCurrentEpoch orders the departing owner's sentinel
   write before the slot is published free; the arriving owner's claim CAS
   reads-from that release store; and the arriving owner's own publish cannot
   hoist above its own CAS. Per-location coherence then leaves the arriving
   owner's publish last, which is the only order that is correct.

   This is the same argument that keeps threadId safe, applied to a field the
   fix was never designed to protect. It falls out of making
   localCurrentEpoch the ownership word and unpublishing it with a release
   store: everything the departing thread did, user words included, is carried
   across the handoff. *)
{ 0:X0=uw; 0:X1=tid; 0:X2=lce; 1:X0=lce; 1:X1=uw; uw=7; tid=3; lce=5; }
 P0            | P1               ;
 MOV X3,#9     | MOV X2,#0        ;
 STR X3,[X0]   | MOV X3,#1        ;
 STR XZR,[X1]  | CASAL X2,X3,[X0] ;
 STLR XZR,[X2] | MOV X4,#8        ;
               | STR X4,[X1]      ;
exists (1:X2=0 /\ uw=9)
